## Summary
Vince Buyssens reviews a draft proposal webpage for X-Bionic, recorded on a local development server. He provides a detailed, section-by-section critique of the design, layout, typography, and narrative flow. His feedback focuses heavily on aligning the visuals with the brand system, improving information architecture, and effectively communicating the core proposition ("The Layer" and automation) through clear, professional diagrams rather than mismatched mockups.

## Segments
[00:00.0-00:17.0] Intro and skipping the About section.
[00:17.0-02:15.0] Critiquing the Intelligence Configuration section for layout and modularity.
[02:15.0-03:40.0] Reviewing the Adoption and Automation section, disliking the low-res look and flow.
[03:40.0-04:10.0] Reviewing the Upstream Time section, pointing out off-brand elements.
[04:10.0-05:29.0] Proposing a new structure for explaining the core proposition and the Layer.
[05:29.0-05:58.0] Discussing narrative flow into the Loop case study.
[05:58.0-07:12.0] Reviewing Loop proof sections and reiterating core feedback.
[07:12.0-09:19.0] Detailed critique of a specific ad card, focusing on AI patterns, typography, and layout.
[09:19.0-09:43.0] Reviewing the marketing Drive card and its typography.
[09:43.0-10:56.2] Concluding remarks on the Enterprise plugin and final summary of priorities.

